---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro"
import DocSection from "../../components/DocSection.astro"

const CONTACT_EMAIL = "me@maxlibin.com"
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "20 May 2026"
---

<Base
  title="homeworkAI — Terms of Use"
  description="The agreement that governs your use of the homeworkAI iOS app: subscriptions, acceptable use, liability."
  pathname="/homeworkai/terms/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", item: "/" },
    { name: "homeworkAI", item: "/homeworkai/" },
    { name: "Terms of Use", item: "/homeworkai/terms/" },
  ]}
>
  <article class="mt-8 mb-16 px-4 md:px-0 max-w-3xl">
    <div class="mb-3 text-sm">
      <a href="/homeworkai/" class="text-fg hover:underline">
        ← homeworkAI
      </a>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-fg mb-2">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint mb-10">Effective {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

    <DocSection title="Agreement">
      <p>
        These Terms of Use ("Terms") are an agreement between you and Max Li
        Bin, an independent developer based in Singapore ("we", "us"), governing
        your use of the homeworkAI iOS app ("the app").
      </p>
      <p>
        By downloading, installing, or using the app you agree to these Terms
        and to our{" "}
        <a href="/homeworkai/privacy/" class="text-fg hover:underline">
          Privacy Policy
        </a>
        . If you don't agree, please don't use the app.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Who can use the app">
      <p>
        The app is intended to be set up and supervised by a parent or guardian
        who is at least 18 years old. If you are under 18, you may only use the
        app with the involvement of a parent or guardian who agrees to these
        Terms on your behalf.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="What the app does">
      <p>
        homeworkAI lets you scan or type a homework question and returns a
        step-by-step explanation generated by AI. Answers are produced by large
        language models and are intended to support learning. They can be wrong,
        incomplete, or out of date. Always check important answers — the app is
        a study aid, not a substitute for a teacher.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Subscriptions and billing">
      <p>
        homeworkAI is free to use with a daily scan limit. Plus is an
        auto-renewing subscription (monthly or yearly) sold and managed by Apple
        via the App Store.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>
          Payment is charged to your Apple ID at confirmation of purchase.
        </li>
        <li>
          The subscription automatically renews for the same period unless
          auto-renew is turned off at least 24 hours before the end of the
          current period.
        </li>
        <li>
          The renewal charge is taken within 24 hours before the period ends.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can manage and cancel your subscription in Settings → Apple ID →
          Subscriptions on your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          Refunds (if any) are handled by Apple under the App Store's standard
          refund policy.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Acceptable use">
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>
          Use the app for cheating in supervised exams or in any way that
          violates your school's academic rules.
        </li>
        <li>
          Upload content that is illegal, infringes someone else's rights, or
          contains personal information about another person without their
          permission.
        </li>
        <li>
          Attempt to reverse-engineer, scrape, or otherwise abuse the app or our
          backend, or to use it in a way that disrupts the service for other
          users.
        </li>
        <li>Use the app to develop a competing product.</li>
      </ul>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Your content">
      <p>
        You keep all rights to the homework photos and questions you submit. You
        grant us a limited, worldwide, royalty-free license to process that
        content for the sole purpose of operating the app — generating an
        answer, displaying your history, and improving reliability.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Intellectual property">
      <p>
        The app, its design, branding, and code are owned by Max Li Bin and are
        protected by intellectual-property laws. We grant you a personal,
        non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to use the app on
        Apple devices you own or control, in accordance with these Terms and
        Apple's standard EULA for App Store apps.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Disclaimers">
      <p>
        The app is provided "as is" and "as available". To the maximum extent
        permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied,
        including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
        non-infringement. AI-generated answers may be wrong; you are responsible
        for verifying them.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Limitation of liability">
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, we will not be liable for any
        indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages
        arising out of or relating to your use of the app. Our total liability
        for any claim arising out of or relating to these Terms is limited to
        the amount you paid us (via Apple) in the 12 months before the claim
        arose, or, if you have not paid us anything, USD 50.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Termination">
      <p>
        You can stop using the app at any time by deleting it. We may suspend or
        terminate your access to the app if you breach these Terms or if
        continuing the service becomes commercially or legally impractical.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Changes to these Terms">
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. We'll change the effective
        date above and, for material changes, surface a notice in the app.
        Continuing to use the app after a change means you accept the updated
        Terms.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Governing law">
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of Singapore, without regard to its
        conflict-of-laws rules. The courts of Singapore have exclusive
        jurisdiction over any dispute arising from these Terms, except where
        your local consumer-protection laws require otherwise.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Apple-specific terms">
      <p>
        You acknowledge that these Terms are between you and us, not Apple, and
        that Apple is not responsible for the app or its content. To the extent
        these Terms are inconsistent with Apple's standard EULA for App Store
        apps, the terms more protective of you apply. Apple and its subsidiaries
        are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them
        against you.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Contact">
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms?{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-fg hover:underline">
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>
      </p>
    </DocSection>
  </article>
</Base>
